{
  "path": "$PRJ/tests/corpus/opentitan/prim_lfsr.sv",
  "modules": [
    {
      "name": "prim_lfsr",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "LfsrType",
          "default": "\"GAL_XOR\"",
          "comment": [
            "Lfsr width"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ptype": "unsigned",
          "name": "LfsrDw",
          "default": "32",
          "comment": [
            "Derived parameter, do not override"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ptype": "unsigned",
          "name": "EntropyDw",
          "default": "8",
          "comment": [
            "Width of output tap (from lfsr_q[StateOutDw-1:0])"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ptype": "unsigned",
          "name": "StateOutDw",
          "default": "8",
          "comment": [
            "Lfsr reset state, must be nonzero!"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ptype": "logic",
          "name": "DefaultSeed",
          "dim": "[LfsrDw-1:0]",
          "default": "LfsrDw'(1)",
          "comment": [
            "Custom polynomial coeffs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ptype": "logic",
          "name": "CustomCoeffs",
          "dim": "[LfsrDw-1:0]",
          "default": "'0",
          "comment": [
            "If StatePermEn is set to 1, the custom permutation specified via StatePerm is applied to the",
            "state output, in order to break linear shifting patterns of the LFSR. Note that this",
            "permutation represents a way of customizing the LFSR via a random netlist constant. This is",
            "different from the NonLinearOut feature below which just transforms the output non-linearly",
            "with a fixed function. In most cases, designers should consider enabling StatePermEn as it",
            "comes basically \"for free\" in terms of area and timing impact. NonLinearOut on the other hand",
            "has area and timing implications and designers should consider whether the use of that feature",
            "is justified."
          ]
        },
        {
          "ptype": "bit",
          "name": "StatePermEn",
          "default": "1'b0"
        },
        {
          "ptype": "logic",
          "name": "StatePerm",
          "dim": "[LfsrDw-1:0][LfsrIdxDw-1:0]",
          "default": "'0",
          "comment": [
            "Enable this for DV, disable this for long LFSRs in FPV"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ptype": "bit",
          "name": "MaxLenSVA",
          "default": "1'b1",
          "comment": [
            "Can be disabled in cases where seed and entropy",
            "inputs are unused in order to not distort coverage",
            "(the SVA will be unreachable in such cases)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ptype": "bit",
          "name": "LockupSVA",
          "default": "1'b1"
        },
        {
          "ptype": "bit",
          "name": "ExtSeedSVA",
          "default": "1'b1",
          "comment": [
            "Introduce non-linearity to lfsr output. Note, unlike StatePermEn, this feature is not \"for",
            "free\". Please double check that this feature is indeed required. Also note that this feature",
            "is only available for LFSRs that have a power-of-two width greater or equal 16bit."
          ]
        },
        {
          "ptype": "bit",
          "name": "NonLinearOut",
          "default": "1'b0"
        }
      ],
      "ports": [
        {
          "direction": "input",
          "name": "clk_i"
        },
        {
          "direction": "input",
          "name": "rst_ni"
        },
        {
          "direction": "input",
          "name": "seed_en_i",
          "comment": [
            "load external seed into the state (takes precedence)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "direction": "input",
          "name": "seed_i",
          "dim": "[LfsrDw-1:0]",
          "comment": [
            "external seed input"
          ]
        },
        {
          "direction": "input",
          "name": "lfsr_en_i",
          "comment": [
            "enables the LFSR"
          ]
        },
        {
          "direction": "input",
          "name": "entropy_i",
          "dim": "[EntropyDw-1:0]",
          "comment": [
            "additional entropy to be XOR'ed into the state"
          ]
        },
        {
          "direction": "output",
          "ptype": "logic",
          "name": "state_o",
          "dim": "[StateOutDw-1:0]",
          "comment": [
            "(partial) LFSR state output"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "localparams": [
        {
          "ptype": "unsigned",
          "name": "LfsrIdxDw",
          "default": "$clog2(LfsrDw)",
          "comment": [
            "Width of the entropy input to be XOR'd into state (lfsr_q[EntropyDw-1:0])"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ptype": "unsigned",
          "name": "LUT_OFF",
          "default": "3"
        },
        {
          "ptype": "logic",
          "name": "LFSR_COEFFS",
          "dim": "[167:0]",
